OL,2,V55555555]U~#hw}h77}jw=hw}j5~c1~k4 %w5s5
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5]U+,*%/*%%/*% *%/*%+.!/*%   %-$
OL,5, Labour continued to defend its
OL,6, controversial TV broadcast on the NHS
OL,7, as the row with the Tories hotted up.
OL,9, The film, using actors, compared a girl
OL,10, who had to wait 11 months for an NHS
OL,11, operation with another who had private
OL,12, treatment within days.
OL,14, Mr Kinnock dismissed accusations of
OL,15, exploiting children and said the girl's
OL,16, parents knew the case would be used.
OL,18, Party campaign coordinator Jack
OL,19, Cunningham said the child's father
OL,20, wanted it conveyed to the public
OL,21, "because he was so angry".
OL,23,F]EFrom 25-03-92 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49605
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774403311
OL,1,V7w3s7s35]                         A5/12
OL,2,V55555555]U~#hw}h77}jw=hw}j5~c1~k4 %w5s5
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5]U+,*%/*%%/*% *%/*%+.!/*%   %-$
OL,5, The Tories mounted a furious attack on
OL,6, Labour's TV film, which showed a girl
OL,7, having to wait for treatment as her
OL,8, parents could not afford private care.
OL,10, Tory Party chairman Chris Patten said
OL,11, on BBC Radio that it was a "sleazy,
OL,12, contemptible" broadcast.
OL,14, Health Secretary William Waldegrave
OL,15, told ITN Mr Kinnock had left his health
OL,16, spokesman Robin Cook "swinging in the
OL,17, wind" to answer for an untrue story.
OL,19, Consultant in the case, Alan Ardouin,
OL,20, rejected the central theme, saying an
OL,21, administrative error had caused the
OL,22, 11-month delay in the girl's operation.
OL,23,F]EFrom 25-03-92 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
