OL,2,V55555555CABC LOSES LOCKERBIE
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CTAPES COURT BID
OL,5, ABC News and a journalist have lost a
OL,6, court bid to avoid handing over to UK
OL,7, police video interviews of two Libyans
OL,8, charged with the Lockerbie bombing.
OL,10, Two High Court judges ruled there was
OL,11, "nothing unlawful" in a Middlesex Crown
OL,12, Court order under anti-terrorist laws
OL,13, to deliver up the tapes.
OL,15, The American TV network and newsman
OL,16, Pierre Salinger said they would comply
OL,17, with a deadline of noon on Thursday for
OL,18, them to be handed over.
OL,20, But the Americans claimed "victory" as
OL,21, judges laid down "radical" guidelines
OL,22, for use of such orders in future.
OL,23,F]DFrom 25-03-92 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
