OL,1,V7w3s7s35                         G12/12
OL,2,V55555555CSCIENTISTS CLAIM
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CA PRIME SUCCESS
OL,5, A team of scientists claims to have
OL,6, found the world's largest prime number,
OL,7, which can be divided by 1 or itself.
OL,9, The number has 227,832 digits and is
OL,10, written as 2^756839-1, which is 2
OL,11, multiplied by itself 756839 times,
OL,12, minus 1.
OL,14, The Atomic Energy Authority scientists
OL,15, at Harwell also claim a new perfect
OL,16, number (2^756839-1) x 2^756838, which
OL,17, has 455,663 digits.
OL,19, A perfect number equals the sum of its
OL,20, factors: 6 is a perfect number as it
OL,21, equals the total of 1, 2 and 3.
OL,23,F]DFrom 25-03-92 / teletextarchive.com
